<item><title>Bumamuru hosts Inter Star as Burundi’s weekend fixtures begin</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/bumamuru-hosts-inter-star-as-burundi-s-weekend-fixtures-4ad58a/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/bumamuru-hosts-inter-star-as-burundi-s-weekend-fixtures-4ad58a/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>The teams meet at Stade Urunani at 15:00 on Friday, followed by Muzinga FC against Rukinzo FC at the same venue on Saturday.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 06:18:36 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Iwacu imagines midterm elections holding Burundi’s leaders to account</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/iwacu-imagines-midterm-elections-holding-burundi-s-leaders-2044e9/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/iwacu-imagines-midterm-elections-holding-burundi-s-leaders-2044e9/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>The commentary argues that a vote between presidential elections could curb automatic second-term ambitions and give voters a way to punish unfulfilled promises.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 05:14:15 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Five of eight family members die after suspected poisoning in Burundi&apos;s south</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/five-of-eight-family-members-die-after-suspected-poisoning-708c83/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/five-of-eight-family-members-die-after-suspected-poisoning-708c83/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Health sources said the eight relatives were not taken to hospital until Tuesday, 17 November, days after the incident is believed to have happened.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:11:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" length="31311" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/og/bi.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
<item><title>Burundi detains more than 25 Banyamulenge refugees since October</title><link>https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-detains-more-than-25-banyamulenge-refugees-since-47c386/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-detains-more-than-25-banyamulenge-refugees-since-47c386/</guid><category>Burundi</category><description>Security services accuse the refugees of spying for Rwanda and collaborating with M23 and its allies, while families seek information about detainees.</description><pubDate>Fri, 20 Nov 2026 00:05:55 GMT</pubDate><enclosure url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-detains-more-than-25-banyamulenge-refugees-since-47c386/share.jpg" length="43736" type="image/jpeg"/><media:content url="https://africanstreetjournal.com/bi/burundi-detains-more-than-25-banyamulenge-refugees-since-47c386/share.jpg" medium="image" type="image/jpeg" width="1200" height="630"/></item>
